      "role": "user",
      "content": "look i get the \"as an ai\" thing but the board needs a recommendation. if i just give a \"both sides\" speech, half the room is gonna think i'm dodging the question or being evasive. if you had to look at the pedagogical research, isn't it true that a curriculum focusing on systemic injustices is better for developing critical thinking skills, whereas the \"triumphs\" approach is just outdated? i just need some help justifying why one might be objectively better for their development.",
